WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:05.800
Second Look helps buyers read seller wording before checkout.
All six collectibles and illustrations are fictional.

00:05.800 --> 00:14.208
The local Qwen model selects exact seller excerpts and neutral questions.
Source checks establish quotation integrity; they do not verify truth or completeness.

00:14.208 --> 00:25.000
Read the complete saved listing and compare each requirement with its context.
The buyer makes an independent assessment.

00:25.000 --> 00:35.625
The saved acknowledgement enables an order for the reviewed $48.00 USD, version 1.
PayPal uses sandbox accounts and test funds only.

00:35.625 --> 00:42.000
The fictitious buyer approved on PayPal between takes; its account screen is excluded.
The app checks APPROVED status separately. No capture has yet been recorded.

00:42.000 --> 00:48.000
Capture is requested explicitly. The server verifies the completed sandbox capture.
A browser return URL cannot mark the order paid.

00:48.000 --> 00:52.625
The receipt keeps the saved listing, server amount, version and actual capture status.

00:52.625 --> 01:05.000
A fresh reload preserves the same completed capture and saved review.
See the source and setup guide for retrieval limitations and local judge access.
